<title>JAPAN: Matsushita, Toyota battery output seen from autumn.</title>
<headline>Matsushita, Toyota battery output seen from autumn.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Matsushita Electric Industrial Co Ltd said on Thursday that Panasonic EV Energy Co Ltd, a joint venture with Toyota Motor Corp, will begin mass production of batteries for electric cars by this autumn.</p>
<p>The joint venture is spending two billion yen to build a production line with the capacity to make 1,250 nickel-metal hydride batteries a month, Matsushita said.</p>
<p>The joint venture, set up in September 1996, is 60-percent owned by Matsushita and 40-percent owned by the Toyota Motor group.</p>
</text>
